# The seed methods (stage seed, written before any development problem was read; generic schemas of the semantic-decomposition
# inventory and of schema theory: combine, change, compare, vary, group).

# --- add_up
@fpm_add_up_1 fact
  holds fp_method add_up

@fpm_add_up_2 fact
  holds fp_method_achieves add_up find_value

@fpm_add_up_3 fact
  holds fp_method_solver add_up calculate

@fpm_add_up_4 fact
  holds fp_method_text add_up "a total is the sum of parts (combine)"

@fpm_add_up_5 fact
  holds fp_method_seq add_up 1

@fpm_add_up_6 fact
  holds fp_method_added add_up seed

@fpm_add_up_7 fact
  holds fp_method_slot add_up parts numbers

@fpm_add_up_8 fact
  holds fp_slot_text add_up parts "the quantities that add up"

@fpm_add_up_9 fact
  holds fp_slot_many add_up parts

@fpm_add_up_10 fact
  holds fp_method_formula add_up "sum(parts)"


